WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:04.030
- So Donald Trump has been
impeached for the second time.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:07.800
The only president in history
to ever be impeached twice

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.440
and it happened in just over a year

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.640
since the last time that he was impeached,

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.880
though of course he was
acquitted in the Senate.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:15.880
So what does that mean?

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.980
Well, obviously now that
the House has impeached,

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.770
which is effectively the indictment,

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:22.810
now that will be referred to the Senate,

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:24.860
and the Senate will try the case.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.900
Now, unfortunately,
the Senate is in recess

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:27.980
and it's currently being run

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.030
by Senate majority
leader, Mitch McConnell,

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.110
and that's not going to change,

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.610
because Chuck Schumer can't become

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.610
the Senate majority leader

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:36.260
until the democratic senators
from Georgia are seated,

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.870
Kamala Harris' replacement
in California is seated,

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:41.270
and Kamala Harris takes her
place as the Vice President

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.620
to break the 50/50 tie in the Senate.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.900
So that's where we are.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.390
Stay tuned for more
impeachment related legal news

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.583
and as always, I'll see you in court.

